  {
   "text": "Two Lorwyn Eclipsed Commander decks were released together with Lorwyn Eclipsed on January 23, 2026.",
   "scene": 0,
   "section": ""
  },
  {
   "text": "Each deck introduces twelve never-before-seen Commander cards to Magic: The Gathering . New Lorwyn Eclipsed cards with the ECC set code numbered #1-24 (and various extended art versions numbered #25-44) are permitted in the Commander, Legacy, and Vintage formats.",
   "scene": 1,
   "section": "Description"
  },
  {
   "text": "Several reprints in the Commander decks have new art and flavor text, all suited to the Lorwyn Eclipsed theme (ECC #45-63). These, and returning cards with the ECC set code and numbered #64-176 are legal for play in any format where a card with the same name is permitted.",
   "scene": 1,
   "section": "Description"
  },
  {
   "text": "This set features two enemy-colored versions of years-old dual land cycles that previously only existed in allied colors :",
   "scene": 1,
   "section": "Description"
  },
  {
   "text": "Rain-Slicked Copse , the bicycle land",
   "scene": 1,
   "section": "Description"
  },
  {
   "text": "Sodden Verdure , the battle land",
   "scene": 1,
   "section": "Description"
  },
  {
   "text": "Each package contains :",
   "scene": 2,
   "section": "Contents"
  },
  {
   "text": "1 foil Commander with borderless art",
   "scene": 2,
   "section": "Contents"
  },
  {
   "text": "1 additional foil Legendary card with borderless art",
   "scene": 2,
   "section": "Contents"
  },
  {
   "text": "10 double-sided tokens or punch cards",
   "scene": 2,
   "section": "Contents"
  },
  {
   "text": "Collector Booster Sample Packs were phased out for this product.",
   "scene": 2,
   "section": "Contents"
  },
  {
   "text": "Lorwyn Eclipsed Commander has one new cycle of cards, all five of which are contained within the Dance of the Elements deck:",
   "scene": 3,
   "section": "Cycles"
  },
  {
   "text": "Additionally, the members of the battle land ( Sodden Verdure ) and bicycle land ( Rain-Slicked Copse ) mega cycles are printed for the first time in the Dance of the Elements deck.",
   "scene": 3,
   "section": "Cycles"
  },
  {
   "text": "A deck focusing on huge elementals , sacrifice and duplicate . The deck represents the light of Lorwyn.",
